hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1281","Abu Ammar Al-Hussein Ibn Harith, Ya’qub Ibn Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi, and Yusuf Ibn Musa told us, they said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, said: I asked the Mother of the Believers, Aisha, and I said: O Mother of the Believers, how was the work of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? And peace be upon him, was he particular about any of the days? She said: “No, his work was constant, and which of you can do what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was able to do?” This is the wording of the hadith of Abu Ammar, and Yusuf said: “No, his deeds were permanent.” As for Al-Dawraqi, he said: I asked Aisha: How was the prayer? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He did not say: Was he singling out any of the days?"
"1282","From us Muhammad bin Al-Alaa bin Kurayb, from us Abu Usama, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I had a woman from my children. A lion. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered and said: “Who is this?” So I said: So-and-so was remembering from her prayer, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Meh, do what you are able to do, for by God, God does not get bored until you get bored.” She said: The most beloved religion to him was the one whose owner always followed it."
"1283","Ali bin Khashram told us, Issa told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “He loved work.” To the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, as long as he continued, even if it was little, and whenever the Prophet prayed a prayer, he would continue to do it.” Abu Salamah said: Those who are committed to their prayers. Surat Al-Ma'arij, Verse 23"
